# The toolchain every release build of the Terraform provider and the
# infrastructure agent uses, pinned to exact versions in this one place
# (#11464). .github/actions/setup-release-toolchain installs it, and each
# release's notes name it, so a version built again from its tag, weeks
# later, is built the same way and is the same bytes. `go-version: stable`
# and GoReleaser's `~> v2` moved, so it would not have been.
#
# A pin left alone ages a toolchain that builds programs making HTTPS calls,
# so the Release Toolchain Pins workflow checks these every week against
# Go's and each tool's newest release, and keeps one issue open while one is
# behind (Scripts/Release/ReleaseToolchain.js). To move one: change it here,
# in its own pull request, and let the Terraform Provider Generation and
# Infrastructure Agent Test workflows build with it (they install it too, and
# build the provider and the agent twice). Tests/Ops/ReleaseToolchain.test.js
# holds every release build to this file.
#
# Go: an exact release, as go.dev/dl lists it.
GO_VERSION=1.27.4
# GoReleaser, open source distribution: a v2 release, with its v.
GORELEASER_VERSION=v2.20.3
# syft, which writes the infrastructure agent's SBOMs: a newer one writes
# other documents.
SYFT_VERSION=v1.57.2
